              "answers": [
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Donepezil blocks the enzyme that degrades acetylcholine, leading to more acetylcholine in the brain. It delays the deterioration of the brain by about 6 months. Common side effects include GIT symptoms while serious adverse effects include hepatic damage.</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>No, unfortunately in humans, Memantine does not appear to significantly improve neural degeneration&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "tip": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "Memantine improves neural degeneration in humans\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "Memantine decreases the glutamate-mediated overexcitation by blocking the NMDA receptors but comes along with agitation, insomnia, drowsiness, dizziness and GIT disturbances. \n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "Memantine is nephrotoxic, and as such should be taken with plenty of water and should never be taken with other nephrotoxic drugs, for instance NSAIDs. \n"
                }
              ],
